```

How does that elevator decide which floor to visit next?

Everything else is secondary.

And for a 20-minute implementation, I'd explicitly tell the interviewer something like:

> "I'll assume all elevators serve all floors, floor count and elevator count are configured at startup, and I'll abstract away physical door/motor/sensor mechanics. I'll focus on request assignment and elevator scheduling."

That single statement prevents the problem from exploding.

One more subtle distinction that will help you a lot:

```text
